    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d234">

                <pb facs="0387" n="295" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v01/pg295"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/10953a</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        Italy</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Page</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-08-01T16:00:00-04:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">August 1, 1918, 4 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1597. Department’s 1476<anchor n="2" xml:id="d234-f1"/> and your 1764.<anchor
                        n="3" xml:id="d234-f2"/> British and French Governments are proposing to
                    Allied Naval Council a unity of command in the Mediterranean, just as there is
                    now a unity of military command on the western front. The Government of the
                    United States is in entire agreement with this view and instructions have been
                    sent to Admiral Sims to give his support to the proposal to agree upon a single
                    naval commander for the forces in the Mediterranean. <pb facs="0388" n="296"
                        xml:id="pg296"/> Please inform Italian Government of the views held by the
                    Government of the United States.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Polk</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
